{# ============================================================================
   THE FULL PAGE — the one container the report flow lives in (ruled direction A).

   A PAGE, NOT AN OVERLAY. Filing an incident is the most consequential thing this
   product asks anybody to do, and it must not be something a click beside it can
   throw away. A route survives a reload, a dropped connection, a second tab and a
   pasted link; it prints; and it is the same address another module's "file as
   incident" button already points at. The steps are plain headed sections down
   one column — there is room, so nothing has to hide.

   THE SOURCE CARD RIDES AT THE HEAD when the filing came from a record; a
   standalone filing has none. Same page either way.

   A RAIL BESIDE THE FORM. The form is 860px and the screen is not, so the column
   beside it carries the two things the form cannot say for itself: the source
   observation, where there is one, and what the chosen kind asks. The rail stands
   still while the form scrolls past it, and below 1160px it stacks under the form
   (@UhifadhiIncident/report/_rail.html.twig).

   ONE WAY OUT, AND IT IS IN THE FILE BAR. The head carries no way back: a filer
   reads it before they have written anything, and an exit offered there is offered
   where the decision is not being made. Cancel sits beside File, where somebody
   decides whether to go through with the filing, and it says where it goes.

   Parameters: controller, momentController, area, kinds, prefill, answers, blocksMissing, chosen, csrfToken, errors,
               placement, placementKept, placementUrl,
               createUrl, cancelUrl, blockSets, areaLists, checklists
   ========================================================================== #}
{# NO CRUMB HERE. The trail is the shell frame's socket and the page fills it
   once (see @UhifadhiIncident/base.html.twig); a container typing its own would
   print the trail twice. #}
<div class="pghead">
    <div>
        <h1 class="pg">Report an incident</h1>
        <p class="pgsub">What makes the record what it is files an incident — a kind, one line saying what happened, a
            place, and the defining question of every block the category switches on. How bad it
            was, who was involved, what it cost and anything that shows it can be added here or on the record
            afterwards, where the timeline keeps who added what and when.</p>
    </div>
</div>

{# TWO COLUMNS, ONE CONTROLLER. The rail's checklist carries the gate's own marks,
   so the gate has to be able to reach it: the controller wraps the form AND the
   rail. #}
<div class="i-rwrap" {{ stimulus_controller(controller, {placementUrl: placementUrl}) }}>
    <div class="ro-col">
        {% if prefill.hasProvenance %}
            {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_source.html.twig', {prefill: prefill}, with_context: false) }}
        {% endif %}

        {# input and change both bubble, so ONE action on the form re-reads the gate
           whatever the filer typed into. #}
        <form class="ro-form" method="post" action="{{ createUrl }}"
              {{ stimulus_action(controller, 'gate', 'input')|stimulus_action(controller, 'gate', 'change') }}>
            {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_carry.html.twig', {csrfToken: csrfToken, prefill: prefill, errors: errors}, with_context: false) }}

            <div class="ro-sect">
                {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_secthd.html.twig', {n: 1, heading: 'What kind of incident', mark: 'req', markLabel: 'needed to file'}, with_context: false) }}
                {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_kind.html.twig', {controller: controller, kinds: kinds, chosen: chosen}, with_context: false) }}
            </div>

            <div class="ro-sect">
                {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_secthd.html.twig', {n: 2, heading: 'What happened', mark: null, markLabel: null}, with_context: false) }}
                {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_what.html.twig', {controller: controller, momentController: momentController, kinds: kinds, chosen: chosen, prefill: prefill, answers: answers, blockSets: blockSets, areaLists: areaLists, placement: placement, placementKept: placementKept}, with_context: false) }}
            </div>

            {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_gate.html.twig', {controller: controller, chosen: chosen, answers: answers, blocksMissing: blocksMissing, cancelUrl: cancelUrl, blockSets: blockSets, placement: placement}, with_context: false) }}
        </form>
    </div>

    {# THE RULES CARD IS NOT HERE, AND IS NOT ANYWHERE. It restated, as nine mono
       rows at the foot of the page, rules the form was already enforcing in front
       of the reader — which answers are marked, which blocks are drawn, that the
       File control is dead until the gate is answered. A card that repeats the page
       it sits under is a second place for the same truth to be written, and the two
       drift. What filing COSTS is not a restatement, and that line stays where
       somebody reads it before they start: the dashboard's entry card. #}
    {{ include('@UhifadhiIncident/report/_rail.html.twig', {
        controller: controller,
        kinds: kinds,
        chosen: chosen,
        prefill: prefill,
        answers: answers,
        blocksMissing: blocksMissing,
        checklists: checklists,
    }, with_context: false) }}
</div>
